<item><title>Botswana&apos;s diamond naming campaign faces US regulatory hurdle</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-s-diamond-naming-campaign-faces-us-regulatory-3276e3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-s-diamond-naming-campaign-faces-us-regulatory-3276e3/</guid><category>Botswana</category><description>Lab-grown diamond producers are invoking the US Federal Trade Commission&apos;s existing guidance as Botswana seeks to distinguish mined stones from laboratory-made alternatives.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:39:09 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bw.jpg" length="34363" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bw.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Botswana&apos;s road toll reaches 189 deaths, with tire failures uncounted</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-s-road-toll-reaches-189-deaths-with-tire-failures-6a8405/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-s-road-toll-reaches-189-deaths-with-tire-failures-6a8405/</guid><category>Botswana</category><description>Crashes killed 189 people and seriously injured 448 between January and September 2026, including 165 fatal crashes, according to the assistant transport minister.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:34:06 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bw.jpg" length="34363" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bw.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Botswana Power Corporation seeks 33% tariff rise for April 2027</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-power-corporation-seeks-33-tariff-rise-for-april-c31771/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-power-corporation-seeks-33-tariff-rise-for-april-c31771/</guid><category>Botswana</category><description>The proposal would lift average commercial rates from P2.11 to P2.76 per kilowatt-hour, with no government subsidy to cushion customers.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:26:40 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-power-corporation-seeks-33-tariff-rise-for-april-c31771/share.jpg" length="42896" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bw/botswana-power-corporation-seeks-33-tariff-rise-for-april-c31771/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
